{"archetypes":[{"name":"semantic-accuracy","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Docs-only plan makes precise behavioral claims (all-or-nothing semantics, specific function names, redactor pipeline) that directly contradict the originating issue's stated semantics; those claims must be verified against the actual implementation before they are committed as authoritative documentation.","prompt_body":"Verify every behavioral assertion in the plan against the actual implementation code — not the issue body or prior docs. Specifically: (1) confirm that `larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_shared` in `scripts/lib-larch-log.sh` implements directory-level all-or-nothing fail-closed semantics (not per-file skip+warn), and that the rejection triggers listed (non-absolute source, symlink, hardlink, bad basename) are accurately enumerated; (2) confirm the redactor pipeline is `redact-tmpdir-paths.sh | redact-secrets.sh --streaming --state-file <tmp>` as described, not a different invocation; (3) confirm the `*.ndjson`-only basename allowlist and that `.quiet`, `.done`, `.status`, `.surfaced`, `.bc-offset`, `.pid` siblings are indeed not committed; (4) confirm `scripts/design-log-publish.sh` calls the same shared helper rather than a separate codepath. Any discrepancy between the plan's stated semantics and the live code would cause the committed documentation to be wrong from day one. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
